From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: retire only the frames the PSD ring has
 room for

mt7603_release_buffered_frames() takes up to nframes frames off the
station's power-save queue, marks the last one with EOSP for a U-APSD
service period and queues them on the PSD ring with
mt76_tx_queue_skb_raw(), which frees what does not fit. The ring is
shared with the other stations and with the multicast sent after DTIM,
so with 96 frames buffered and 32 ring entries in use the last two
frames were freed, EOSP with them, while the driver still ended the
service period locally: the station lost the frames and kept waiting
for an EOSP that never came.

Only retire as many frames as the ring has room for. The rest stay on
the power-save queue, the TIM bit stays set and the last frame sent
carries more data, so the station picks them up with its next trigger.
With no room at all, nothing is retired and the service period ends as
for an empty queue.

Found by a Codex audit agent (user-space harness running this function
and the DMA raw path): 96 frames with 32 entries in use now queue 94
with EOSP on the last and keep 2 buffered, instead of dropping 2 and
EOSP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/mt7603/main.c
+++ b/mt7603/main.c
@@ -475,18 +475,30 @@
 {
 	struct mt7603_dev *dev = hw->priv;
 	struct mt7603_sta *msta = (struct mt7603_sta *)sta->drv_priv;
+	struct mt76_queue *q = dev->mphy.q_tx[MT_TXQ_PSD];
 	struct sk_buff_head list;
 	struct sk_buff *skb, *tmp, *last;
 	bool eosp_null, uapsd;
 	unsigned long drained;
 	u16 pending = 0;
 	u8 last_tid;
-	int i;
+	int i, room;
 
 	__skb_queue_head_init(&list);
 
 	mt7603_wtbl_set_ps(dev, msta, false);
 
+	/*
+	 * mt76_tx_queue_skb_raw() frees a frame the PSD ring has no room for,
+	 * and the ring is shared with the other stations and the multicast
+	 * after DTIM. Only retire what fits, so that EOSP goes out on a frame
+	 * that is actually queued; the rest stays buffered, with more data
+	 * set, for the next trigger.
+	 */
+	room = q->ndesc - 2 - READ_ONCE(q->queued);
+	if (nframes > room)
+		nframes = max(room, 0);
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->ps_lock);
 	skb_queue_walk_safe(&msta->psq, skb, tmp) {
 		if (!nframes)
